    {
      "tag": "Six",
      "h2": "The Six Basics",
      "body_html": "<p><strong>Rot</strong> (red), <strong>blau</strong> (blue), <strong>grun</strong> (green), <strong>gelb</strong> (yellow), <strong>schwarz</strong> (black), <strong>weiss</strong> (white). Memorise these first.</p>"
    },
    {
      "tag": "More",
      "h2": "More Colours",
      "body_html": "<p>Other common ones: <strong>orange, lila</strong> (purple), <strong>rosa</strong> (pink), <strong>braun</strong> (brown), <strong>grau</strong> (grey).</p>"
    },
    {
      "tag": "Use",
      "h2": "Saying What Colour",
      "body_html": "<p>'Mein T-Shirt ist rot' = 'My T-shirt is red'. Colours stay the same after <strong>ist</strong> (is). They only change when before a noun: 'ein rotes T-Shirt'.</p>"
    }
  ],
